# `volatility::Garch11Params`

Parameters of a plain GARCH(1,1)-in-mean model for pricing: Ngarch11Params without the leverage.

`R_t = r + λ√h_t − ½h_t + √h_t z_t`, `h_{t+1} = ω + β h_t + α h_t z_t²`: the NGARCH of [`Ngarch11Params`](Ngarch11Params.md) with `γ = 0`. The variance is stationary when `α + β < 1 − stationarity_margin`, with long-run level `ω/(1 − α − β)`.

## Fields

### `omega`

`double`, default `0.02`.

Variance intercept, positive.

### `alpha`

`double`, default `0.08`.

Reaction to the shock.

### `beta`

`double`, default `0.90`.

Persistence.

### `lambda`

`double`, default `0.0`.

Risk premium per unit of volatility.

### `r`

`double`, default `0.0`.

Risk-free rate per period.

### `variance_floor`

`double`, default `1e-12`.

Floor under the variance.

### `stationarity_margin`

`double`, default `1e-6`.

Persistence must be below `1 − margin`.

## Guidance

Passed to `pricing_metrics`, `pricing_variance_forecast` and `unconditional_variance`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

`omega`: the long-run variance `ω/(1 − α − β)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  for (const double omega : {0.01, 0.02, 0.04})
    out.writeln("omega", omega, ": unconditional variance", fin::volatility::unconditional_variance(fin::volatility::Garch11Params{.omega = omega}), ", formula", omega / (1.0 - 0.98));
}
```

### Example 2

`alpha` and `beta`: moving mass from `β` to `α` keeps the persistence and the long-run variance but changes how the variance reacts to shocks. Compare the variance after a large return.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <utility>
#include <vector>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const auto cfg = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
  const Series returns = pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03, 0.0});
  for (const auto &[alpha, beta] : std::vector<std::pair<double, double>>{{0.04, 0.94}, {0.15, 0.83}}) {
    const auto m = fin::pricing::pricing_metrics(returns, fin::volatility::Garch11Params{.omega = 2e-6, .alpha = alpha, .beta = beta}, cfg);
    out.writeln("alpha", alpha, "beta", beta, ": variances", m.variance.items<double>());
  }
}
```

### Example 3

`lambda`: the risk premium enters the conditional mean as `λ√h`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto cfg = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
  const Series returns = pluss::make_series({0.001, -0.002, 0.003});
  for (const double lambda : {0.0, 0.1})
    out.writeln("lambda", lambda, ": conditional means", fin::pricing::pricing_metrics(returns, fin::volatility::Garch11Params{.omega = 2e-6, .lambda = lambda}, cfg).mean.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 4

`r`: the risk-free rate per period enters the conditional mean.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto cfg = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
  const Series returns = pluss::make_series({0.001, -0.002, 0.003});
  for (const double r : {0.0, 0.0002})
    out.writeln("r", r, ": conditional means", fin::pricing::pricing_metrics(returns, fin::volatility::Garch11Params{.omega = 2e-6, .r = r}, cfg).mean.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 5

`variance_floor` and `stationarity_margin`: a non-stationary parameter set is refused.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <string>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const fin::volatility::Garch11Params p{.omega = 0.02, .alpha = 0.1, .beta = 0.9};
  try {
    (void)(fin::volatility::unconditional_variance(p));
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find('\n')));
  }
}
```

